course: dictionary
lesson: 5948
title: Mastering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mastering means learning something so well that you can do it easily and without mistakes. «Mastering times tables» means knowing them quickly and getting them right every time. You can also master a feeling, which means getting control of it: «mastering his fear» shows he is no longer ruled by his fear.
explain: Mastering is a verb (master, masters, mastered, mastering) and it can also be a noun for a job. Read the words around it to see which meaning is used, and check your idea by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: «The producer shapes how the record sounds, choosing instruments and making the big decisions; mixing balances the tracks, and mastering is the final polish so it sounds right on phones, speakers and radio.» Words like record, tracks and polish are the clues. Here mastering is a job in a music studio, not a skill you learn at school.
fact: Mastering a skill or subject means learning it completely and becoming really good at it.
fact: Mastering a feeling means getting control of it, as in «mastering his fear».
fact: In music, mastering is the last stage of making a recording, when the sound is balanced and made ready to sell or stream.
fact: Schools often talk about «mastery» when pupils know a skill well, such as their times tables.
fact: Context clues help: if the words around mastering mention music, tracks or a studio, it means the music job.
exercise: «She practised her spellings every day until she had mastered them.» What does mastered mean here? | Read them out loud once only | *Learned them completely and got really good at them | Forgot them all by Friday | Lost the paper they were written on
exercise: «He was shaking, but he took a deep breath and began mastering his fear.» What is he doing? | *Getting control of his fear | Running away from the stage | Telling everyone about his fear | Making his fear bigger
exercise: «The final polish of mastering makes the record sound right on phones and speakers.» In music, what is mastering? | Writing the lyrics of a song | Playing the drums very loudly | The first idea a singer has | *The last stage of making a recording, when the sound is balanced
test: Maya is mastering the violin. What does this mean? | She is throwing her violin away | *She is becoming really good at playing it | She is selling her violin | She is tuning it once and stopping
test: In a story, a boy who is mastering his fear is most likely to be | Asleep | Careless | Angry | *Brave
exam: Which phrase best replaces mastering in «Ella is mastering her times tables»? | *Knowing them completely and quickly | Singing them loudly | Copying them into a book | Forgetting them
